>> title: Baked Turkey Wings
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: turkey, gravy, southern, roast, braise
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: turkey wings, smothered turkey wings, turkey necks, baked turkey wings and gravy
>> servings: 4
>> time: 2 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the lid goes on only after the forty-five minutes uncovered; covered from the start they steam out grey for good
>> pairs-with: onion-gravy, candied-yams, cornbread-dressing, collard-greens
>> washing-up: the roasting tin

>> step: Roast uncovered until the skin has taken colour. The lid goes on only after that.
Roast them uncovered first and put the lid on only once the skin has taken colour.

>> step: season, under the skin too
Season @turkey wings{4%lb}(1.8 kg; split at the joints) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @black pepper{2%tsp}, @paprika{2%tsp}, @garlic powder{2%tsp}, @poultry seasoning{1%tsp}.

>> step: roast uncovered 400°F 45 min
Roast @&(~1)seasoned wings{} on a bed of @yellow onion{1%large}(sliced) at 400°F (205°C) for ~roast{45%min}.

>> step: braise covered 325°F 1 hr 30 min
Braise @&(~1)coloured wings{} covered in @onion gravy{3%cup}(710 mL), @chicken stock{1%cup}(240 mL) at 325°F (165°C) for ~braise{90%min}.

Carve nothing. The wing goes to the plate whole with the gravy over it.
